I wrote `verification-edit.json`. The verdict is **revise**: the Kareem Rahma profile is not ready to release yet, but it needs a wording repair, not new research. I changed no other repo files and published nothing.

**Why it can't release:** the article's "cleanest test" counts Rahma's dread of a desk job as Seven evidence ("a trapped life, not a worthless one"). But when he told Maury Povich (Interview, May 2026) that he hated "sending emails back and forth for a living," his next words were "I'm destined for greater things. I should stand out. I deserve more than being just a cog in the machine." That is Three-shaped. The article quotes part of that answer in its Type 3 section but cuts the "cog" line, and never says the same dread sits in that answer. FAQ 2 uses the same evidence as the deciding reason. Once corrected, Seven's lead rests mostly on the "airplane ride, not the arrival" evidence. That could narrow the call further. If the leading type changes, the run has to be held for a full re-review.

