**What checked out:**
- I reopened 32 of 33 sources this stage, live or through archive and reader copies. The one I couldn't open, the wedding report, isn't used by the article.
- 110 of 111 quotes match the source exactly; the last is the one-word CULTURED variant listed below.
- For the two audio interviews, I ran a third independent machine transcription. It agrees with the first two on every quoted span apart from filler words. That includes "emails until 80" and "about 28", which the editor had left resting on one transcription.
- I agreed with all 45 of the editor's decisions on the reviewers' findings. All 22 passages the reviewers asked to keep survived. No earlier blockers carried over. Source coverage and metadata are complete.

**Six minor fixes to make in the same pass:**
- "a year later" should be "six months later": September 2024 newsletter to March 2025 Rolling Stone.
- The Vice-to-Times move is framed as being for "experiencing all of the things." His stated reason was that the job tripled his salary.
- The CULTURED quote ("what I had perceived") matches a sister URL, not the one cited ("what I perceived").
- The similarity check the editor deferred now trips. One match is a generic Seven definition sentence that should be reworded for him. The other is his own sourced airplane-ride line, which can stay.
- The Harris paragraph is a 188-word wall and should be split.
- The body has only two internal links. Add a link to a related published profile, for example Bourdain, whom Vanity Fair compared him to.

The audio checks are still machine transcription, not a human re-listen. I listed that as a non-blocking research task.
